# Mercedes-Benz S-Class W126 (300SE) four-door saloon, 1979-1991.
#
# The W126 S-Class: 4,995 mm long, 1,820 mm wide, 1,437 mm high, 2,935 mm
# wheelbase (SEL 5,160/3,075); 2.8-5.6 petrol and 3.0/3.5 diesel. The largest
# class-4 saloon parc of the 1980s in Britain, facelifted in 1985.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mercedes-Benz_W126
#
# Colours: Black, Astral Silver, Nautical Blue and Champagne are period
# Mercedes-Benz finishes.
#
# Weight: 50 in total (black 18, silver 15, blue 10, champagne 7), between the
# Jaguar XJ's 60 and the BMW 7 E32's 40.
#
# Speed 230 km/h; comfort 140/540 (line). Classes 3,4.
# Dates: 1979-1991 with a road tail to about 2005.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/mercedes-w126.blend. References:
# citycars/references/mercedes-w126/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

